tery in Valletta, Malta. It was constructed in the 16th century by the Order of Saint John, on or near the site of an Ottoman battery from the Great Siege of Malta. The battery forms the lower tier of St.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Malta_-_Valletta_-_Pjazza_Kastilja_-_Upper_Barrakka_Gardens_-_Saluting_Battery_01_ies.jpg/960px-Malta_-_Valletta_-_Pjazza_Kastilja_-_Upper_Barrakka_Gardens_-_Saluting_Battery_01_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Saluting Battery (Valletta)"},{"n":"Lascaris War Rooms","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.894884,"lo":14.512782,"d":432,"w":"https://www.lascariswarrooms.com/","wp":"en:Lascaris War Rooms","wd":"Q1648164","ds":"The Lascaris War Rooms are an underground complex of tunnels and chambers in Valletta, Malta that housed the War Headquarters from where the defence of the island was conducted during the Second World War. The rooms were later used by NATO and are now open to the public as a museum.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Lascaris_War_Room_Entrance.jpg/960px-Lascaris_War_Room_Entrance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Lascaris War Rooms"},{"n":"Barrakka Lift","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":35.894319,"lo":14.511977,"d":444,"wp":"en:Barrakka Lift","wd":"Q20503060","ds":"The Barrakka Lift is a lift in Valletta, Malta which was constructed in 2012, on the site of a previous lift which had operated from 1905 to 1973 and which was demolished in 1983. It is located inside the ditch of the fortifications of Valletta, and links Lascaris Wharf to St. Peter and Paul Bastion and the Upper Barrakka Gardens.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Malta_-_Valletta_-_Xatt_Lascaris%2BUpper_Barrakka_Lift_%28MSTHC%29_01_ies.jpg/960px-Malta_-_Valletta_-_Xatt_Lascaris%2BUpper_Barrakka_Lift_%28MSTHC%29_01_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Barrakka Lift"},{"n":"Saint Barbara Bastion","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":35.896447,"lo":14.514597,"d":510,"wp":"en:St. Barbara Bastion","wd":"Q104864518","ds":"Close to the Valletta Grand Harbour, St. Barbara Bastion is a flat-faced bastion with a low parapet overlooking the Grand Harbour Area, Valletta, Malta.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/St_Barbara_Bastion.jpg/960px-St_Barbara_Bastion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"St. Barbara Bastion"},{"n":"Art by the Seaside Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":35.887529,"lo":14.518182,"d":534,"w":"https://seasideart.com.mt/","ad":"16 Triq il-Mina tax-Xatt"},{"n":"Malta Time-Gun Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.895299,"lo":14.511617,"d":538,"w":"https://www.wirtartna.org/maltatimegunmuseum","ad":"Misraħ Kastilja"},{"n":"Luciano Al Porto Boutique","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":35.896443,"lo":14.513591,"d":539,"wd":"Q111873412","ad":"255 St. Ursula Street","wifi":1},{"n":"Wreck of SS Margit","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":35.890482,"lo":14.522715,"d":627},{"n":"Underground Valletta","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.897069,"lo":14.512659,"d":638,"w":"https://heritagemalta.mt/explore/underground-valletta/","ad":"Triq il-Merkanti"},{"n":"MUŻA - National Art Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.896293,"lo":14.511262,"d":640,"h":"Jan-Feb: Mo,We-Su 09:00-17:00, Tu off; Mar-Oct: Mo-Su 10:00-18:00; Nov-Dec: Mo-Su 09:00-17:00","w":"https://muza.mt/","ad":"Triq il-Merkanti","f":["wc"]},{"n":"Spazju Kreattiv","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":35.895609,"lo":14.510438,"d":641,"h":"Tu-Fr 09:00-21:00; Sa-Su 10:00-21:00","w":"https://kreattivita.org/en/","ph":"+356 2122 3200","ad":"Misraħ Kastilja"},{"n":"Auberge d'Italie","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":35.896482,"lo":14.511393,"d":648,"wp":"en:Auberge d'Italie","wd":"Q16863312","ds":"The Auberge d'Italie (Maltese: Berġa tal-Italja, Italian: Albergo d'Italia) is an auberge in Valletta, Malta. It was built in various stages in the late 16th century to house knights of the Order of Saint John from the langue of Italy, and it originally had a Mannerist design by Girolamo Cassar and several other architects.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Auberge_d%27Italie%2C_Valletta_003.jpg/960px-Auberge_d%27Italie%2C_Valletta_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Auberge d'Italie"},{"n":"Cathedral Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.89733,"lo":14.512778,"d":659,"w":"https://stjohnscocathedral.com/","wd":"Q111994210","ad":"Triq il-Merkanti"},{"n":"Palazzo Consiglia","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":35.897942,"lo":14.515969,"d":660,"w":"http://palazzoconsiglia.com/","ph":"+35621244222","wd":"Q111873420","ad":"102 Triq Saint Ursula","f":["ac"],"wifi":1},{"n":"Saint James Cavalier","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.895809,"lo":14.510298,"d":665,"h":"Tu-Su 09:00-21:00","w":"https://stjamescavalier.com/","ph":"+356 2122 3200","wd":"Q7401400","ad":"Pjazza Kastilja","f":["free"]},{"n":"Palazzo Paolina Boutique Hotel","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":35.897946,"lo":14.515035,"d":666,"wd":"Q111873418","ad":"101 Triq San Pawl","wifi":1},{"n":"Pjazza tal-Belt Vittoriosa","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":35.887905,"lo":14.521773,"d":691},{"n":"31st March 1979 - Freedom Day","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":35.887167,"lo":14.520997,"d":701},{"n":"Saint John's Co-Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":35.897697,"lo":14.512623,"d":702,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:30-16:30; Sa 09:30-12:30; Su,PH off","w":"https://stjohnscocathedral.com/","ph":"+356 2122 0536","wp":"en:Saint John's Co-Cathedral","wd":"Q613619","ad":"Triq San Ġwann","f":["wc"],"ds":"St John's Co-Cathedral (Maltese: Kon-Katidral ta' San Ġwann) is a Catholic co-cathedral in Valletta, Malta, dedicated to Saint John the Baptist. It was built by the Order of St. John between 1573 and 1578, having been commissioned by Grand Master Jean de la Cassière as the Conventual Church of Saint John (Maltese: Knisja Konventwali ta' San Ġwann).","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/St_John%27s_Co-Cathedral%2C_Valletta_001.jpg/960px-St_John%27s_Co-Cathedral%2C_Valletta_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"St John's Co-Cathedral"},{"n":"Saint Joseph Oratory","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.887641,"lo":14.52176,"d":710,"h":"Mo-Su 09:30-12:00"},{"n":"Auberge d’Auvergne et de Provence","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":35.888463,"lo":14.52258,"d":711,"wp":"en:Auberge d'Auvergne et Provence","wd":"Q16252175","ds":"Auberge d'Auvergne et Provence (Maltese: Berġa ta' Alvernja u Provenza) is an auberge in Birgu, Malta. It was built to house knights of the Order of Saint John from the langues of Auvergne and Provence. Auberge d'Auvergne et Provence was built in the 1530s, incorporating earlier buildings.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Auberge_d%27_Auvergne_et_Provence_01.jpg/960px-Auberge_d%27_Auvergne_et_Provence_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Auberge d'Auvergne et Provence"},{"n":"Esplora","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.891947,"lo":14.524006,"d":721,"h":"Tu-Fr 09:30-16:00; Sa 10:30-05:00; Su 11:30-06:00","w":"https://www.esplora.org.mt/","ph":"25401900","ad":"Triq Marina","wifi":1},{"n":"Villa Bighi","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":35.892862,"lo":14.524037,"d":730,"ds":"Royal Naval Hospital Bighi (RNH Bighi) also known as Bighi Hospital, was a major naval hospital located in the small town of Kalkara on the island of Malta. It was built on the site of the gardens of Palazzo Bichi, that was periodically known as Palazzo Salvatore.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Villa_Bighi_aerial_view%2C_2026_%28first_angle%29.jpg/960px-Villa_Bighi_aerial_view%2C_2026_%28first_angle%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa