,"ad":"72 Triq Tigné","f":["card"]},{"n":"HSBC","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":35.873208,"lo":14.518854,"d":2105},{"n":"GO","g":"essentials","k":"mobile_phone","la":35.909351,"lo":14.506469,"d":2111},{"n":"HSBC","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":35.888113,"lo":14.492793,"d":2134},{"n":"Alpha Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":35.873578,"lo":14.523093,"d":2145},{"n":"Plaza","g":"essentials","k":"mall","la":35.909734,"lo":14.506077,"d":2164,"wifi":1},{"n":"Lower Barrakka Gardens","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":35.8975,"lo":14.517778,"d":632,"ds":"The Lower Barrakka Gardens (Maltese: Il-Barrakka t'Isfel) are a public garden in Valletta, Malta, twinned with the Upper Barrakka Gardens in the same city. The gardens have a view of the Grand Harbour and the breakwater. It includes the Monument to Sir Alexander Ball, which is a prominent feature in the form of a neoclassical temple located in the centre of the garden.","wpu":"Lower Barrakka Gardens","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Vallettaupperbarraccagardens.JPG/960px-Vallettaupperbarraccagardens.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Basilica of the Nativity of Mary, Senglea","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":35.88563,"lo":14.51803,"d":731,"ds":"The Basilica of the Nativity of Mary or Basilica of Our Lady of Victories is a Roman Catholic parish church located at Senglea, Malta. It is dedicated to the Nativity of the Virgin Mary.","wpu":"Basilica of the Nativity of Mary, Senglea","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Sudika_Isla_basilica.jpg/960px-Sudika_Isla_basilica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"War Memorial (Floriana)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":35.893653,"lo":14.508114,"d":733,"ds":"The War Memorial (Maltese: Monument tal-Gwerra) is a memorial obelisk in Floriana, Malta, which commemorates the dead of World War I and World War II. It was inaugurated on 11 November 1938 by Governor Charles Bonham-Carter to the memory of those killed in World War I, but in 1949 it was rededicated to those killed in both world wars.","wpu":"War Memorial (Floriana)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Monumento_a_la_guerra%2C_Floriana%2C_isla_de_Malta%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-25%2C_DD_177.jpg/960px-Monumento_a_la_guerra%2C_Floriana%2C_isla_de_Malta%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-25%2C_DD_177.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Valletta Waterfront","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":35.89,"lo":14.508056,"d":749,"ds":"The Valletta Waterfront, is a promenade in Floriana, Malta, mainly featuring three prominent buildings: a church in the middle, the Pinto Stores or the Pinto Wharf on the left, and the Forni Stores or the Forni Shopping Complex on the right. The buildings were originally stores and warehouses, built in the 18th century, and the design is attributed to Andrea Belli.","wpu":"Valletta Waterfront","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/3_Valletta_waterfront_090917.jpg/960px-3_Valletta_waterfront_090917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"City Gate (Valletta)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":35.896111,"lo":14.509167,"d":766,"ds":"City Gate (Maltese: Bieb il-Belt, literally \"Door of the City\") is a gate located at the entrance of Valletta, Malta. The present gate, which is the fifth one to have stood on the site, was built between 2011 and 2014 to designs of the Italian architect Renzo Piano. The first gate which stood on the site was Porta San Giorgio, which was built in 1569 to designs of either Francesco Laparelli or Girolamo Cassar.","wpu":"City Gate (Valletta)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/City_Gate%2C_Valletta_002.jpg/960px-City_Gate%2C_Valletta_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tritons' Fountain","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":35.895639,"lo":14.508278,"d":804,"ds":"The Tritons' Fountain (Maltese: Il-Funtana tat-Tritoni) is a fountain located in Floriana, Malta. It consists of three bronze Tritons holding up a large basin, balanced on a concentric base built out of concrete and clad in 730 tons of travertine slabs. The fountain is one of Malta's most important Modernist landmarks.","wpu":"Tritons' Fountain","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Triton_Fountain_in_2018_02.jpg/960px-Triton_Fountain_in_2018_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Valletta , also known as Città Umilissima (transl. the Humblest City), is the capital city of Malta and one of its 68 council areas. Located between the Grand Harbour to the east and Marsamxett Harbour to the west, its population as of 2021 was 5,157. As Malta's capital city, it is a commercial centre for shopping, bars, dining, and café life.","wpu":"Valletta","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/St_Sebastian_Curtain_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-St_Sebastian_Curtain_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}